  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations and intermittent lightheadedness in the setting of known unspecified atrial fibrillation (I48.91). Given the personal history of transient ischemic attack and cerebral infarction, prolonged cardiac rhythm monitoring via external cardiac event monitoring (CPT 93271) is clinically indicated to evaluate for arrhythmia burden and guide anticoagulation management. This service is medically necessary to document the frequency and duration of atrial fibrillation episodes and to inform stroke risk assessment in a patient with a prior cerebrovascular event."
